🎯 Attack Logic (The Hacker's Trick)

The Blueprint: The attacker crafts a malicious XLS document that contains no standard VBA macros, allowing it 
to bypass modern security configurations and traditional antivirus solutions that strictly scan for VBA code.

The Mechanism: Instead of VBA, the file leverages ancient Excel 4.0 Macros (XLM). The script is configured to
trigger automatically upon opening, silently download a malicious payload (Iroto.dll), execute it in the 
background, and hide the worksheets containing the formula logic from the user's view.

🕵️‍♂️ Investigation Process (How to Spot It)
File Validation: Verify the file type, structure, and known reputation across global threat intelligence databases.
Structural Inspection: Analyze the Object Linking and Embedding (OLE) structure to detect ancient macro sheets or
automated execution flags.
Deobfuscation & Extract: Uncover hidden or heavily obscured cells and worksheets to extract the hidden execution 
formulas and command-and-control (C2) domains.


